findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted duplicate axiathon-core in dependencies but did not flag
    the 6 inline version specs vs workspace = true pattern. Dev added chrono and uuid
    with inline versions.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[LOW] #[non_exhaustive] missing on ApiError enum \u2014\
    \ error.rs:12' citing rust.md rules. While this is on ApiError not FieldErrorCode\
    \ specifically, the principle was caught. However, FieldErrorCode was not specifically\
    \ mentioned, so this is a partial catch at best."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted trace_id is 'just a random UUID unconnected to any tracing
    infrastructure' under the observability HIGH finding, but did not specifically
    flag the hardcoded 'none' string in ResponseMeta. The issue was adjacent but not
    directly identified.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] Zero observability \u2014 no tracing usage anywhere'\
    \ noting tracing/tracing-subscriber are declared but never imported, no #[instrument]\
    \ annotations, no structured logging on auth failures or rate limit hits."
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that a SECURITY comment claims errors are 'logged for
    debugging' when no logging exists. The reviewer caught zero observability but
    did not call out the misleading security comment specifically.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA did not write a test for non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header.
    No phase addressed this edge case.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-209 security tests (security.rs) checking for no internal\
    \ paths/crate names/stack traces in errors, but the pipeline output does not indicate\
    \ response body content assertions were included \u2014 only status code checks\
    \ are described."
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] No CORS configuration' noting no CORS middleware
    or headers exist, but TEA did not write CORS header verification tests. The reviewer
    caught the missing CORS but not the specific test gap of checking only status
    codes.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since no structured logging was implemented (I4), the wrong-log-level
    issue never arose. No phase preemptively specified that 4xx should use warn! vs
    error! for 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted '[MEDIUM] No CORS configuration' as missing entirely, but
    did not flag CWE-942 or the Any origin/method/header permissiveness risk. Since
    CORS was never implemented, the overly-permissive configuration issue was not
    encountered.
